Replace the file-backed dynamic dependency lists with the static set of
packages the imported module closure (nemo_skills.pipeline.cli,
pipeline.utils.*, pipeline.nemo_rl.* as consumed by nvflow) actually
requires. The upstream blanket lists (core/requirements.txt,
requirements/pipeline.txt) pull in a ~40-package benchmark suite,
including git-only packages (compute-eval, evalplus, koifeval at the
time) and hard pins (litellm==1.83.14, click<8.2) that are neither
imported by the pipeline entry points nor satisfiable against the
Gentoo tree. The benchmark/model-client deps remain lazy imports and
must be installed by hand if a benchmark pipeline is run.

The tools/core/pipeline/dev extras were dropped along with the dynamic
optional-dependencies: they reference the same unresolvable files.

